.\" bootcontrold(8) man page
.\" To preview: man -l docs/man/bootcontrold.8
.\" Install to /usr/share/man/man8/bootcontrold.8 via the .deb / .rpm rules.
.TH BOOTCONTROLD 8 "2026-05-20" "BootControl 0.1.0" "System Administration"

.SH NAME
bootcontrold \- privileged D-Bus backend for BootControl

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bootcontrold

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bootcontrold
is the privileged backend daemon for BootControl. It serves the
.B org.bootcontrol.Manager
interface on D\-Bus and is the only component that ever opens
.IR /etc/default/grub ,
.IR /boot/loader/entries/ ,
.IR /etc/kernel/cmdline
or
.I /sys/firmware/efi/efivars/
for writing.

The daemon is
.B socket-activated
by systemd: nothing runs until a frontend (\fBbootcontrol\fR(1),
\fBbootcontrol-tui\fR(1) or \fBbootcontrol-gui\fR(1)) makes the first
D\-Bus call. It exits after an idle window so the box pays no continuous
overhead.

Every mutating method enforces, in order:
.IP 1. 4
.B Immutable-distro pre-flight
\(em on rpm-ostree / ostree / SteamOS / NixOS / Vanilla OS hosts the
daemon refuses naive writes that would either fail on a read-only mount
or be discarded on the next rebase, and (on rpm-ostree) transparently
delegates the kernel-cmdline operations to
.BR "rpm-ostree kargs" .
.IP 2. 4
.B Polkit
authorisation against the per-method action.
.IP 3. 4
.B ETag freshness
verification under the file's
.BR flock (2).
.IP 4. 4
.B Snapshot
of every file touched by the operation, written to the snapshot root
with a manifest. The operation fails closed if the snapshot fails.
.IP 5. 4
.B Sanitization
of any payload that ends up on the kernel command line (blacklist:
\fBinit=\fR, \fBselinux=0\fR, \fBapparmor=0\fR, \fBmodule_blacklist=\fR,
…).
.IP 6. 4
.B Atomic write
via
.IR file.tmp
\+
.BR rename (2).
.IP 7. 4
.B Failsafe entry
re-injection after every successful GRUB write so a misbehaving main
config still leaves a recoverable fallback.
.IP 8. 4
.B Audit log
to journald with structured fields (MESSAGE_ID, OPERATION, TARGET_PATHS,
ETAG_BEFORE/AFTER, SNAPSHOT_ID, CALLER_UID, POLKIT_ACTION).

The daemon never reads frontend code and never re-exposes its internal
filesystem API outside D\-Bus.

.SH RUNNING
The daemon is normally launched by socket activation:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo systemctl enable --now bootcontrold.socket
.fi
.RE
.PP
That binds
.I /run/bootcontrold.sock
and lets D\-Bus auto-start the daemon when
.B org.bootcontrol.Manager
is first requested.
.PP
For local development you can run the binary directly. Use environment
overrides to point at non-system paths:
.PP
.RS
.nf
BOOTCONTROL_BUS=session \\
BOOTCONTROL_GRUB_PATH=/tmp/grub \\
BOOTCONTROL_FAILSAFE_PATH=/tmp/failsafe.cfg \\
BOOTCONTROL_SNAPSHOT_ROOT=/tmp/snapshots \\
  ./target/debug/bootcontrold
.fi
.RE

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BOOTCONTROL_BUS
Set to
.B session
to bind to the user's session bus (CI / E2E tests). Anything else / unset
binds to the system bus.
.TP
.B BOOTCONTROL_GRUB_PATH
Override the path to
.IR /etc/default/grub .
E2E tests only.
.TP
.B BOOTCONTROL_FAILSAFE_PATH
Override the failsafe snippet output path. E2E tests only.
.TP
.B BOOTCONTROL_SNAPSHOT_ROOT
Override the snapshot root directory (default:
.IR /var/lib/bootcontrol/snapshots ).
Required when running the daemon as an unprivileged user.
.TP
.B BOOTCONTROL_IMMUTABLE_DISTRO_OVERRIDE
Force the host classification to
.BR ostree ,
.BR rpm-ostree ,
.BR steamos ,
.BR nixos
or
.BR vanilla-os ,
bypassing all filesystem probes. Used by E2E tests to exercise the
rejection / delegation paths on a classic host.
.TP
.B BOOTCONTROL_VCONSOLE_PATH
Override the
.IR /etc/vconsole.conf
path used by the LUKS keymap pre-flight check.
.TP
.B BOOTCONTROL_KBD_KEYMAP_DIRS
Colon-separated list of kbd data directories scanned by the LUKS
keymap pre-flight. The default colon-joins, in order:
.IR /usr/share/kbd/keymaps ,
.IR /usr/lib/kbd/keymaps ,
.IR /usr/share/keymaps ,
.IR /lib/kbd/keymaps .
.TP
.B BOOTCONTROL_EFIVARS_DIR
Override the efivarfs mount point used by the cross-platform UEFI
variable reader (default:
.IR /sys/firmware/efi/efivars ).
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Verbosity filter for
.BR tracing-subscriber .

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/bin/bootcontrold
The daemon binary.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/bootcontrold.service
systemd unit definition.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/bootcontrold.socket
systemd socket activation unit.
.TP
.I /run/bootcontrold.sock
The activation socket.
.TP
.I /usr/share/dbus-1/system.d/org.bootcontrol.Manager.conf
D\-Bus system policy.
.TP
.I /usr/share/dbus-1/system-services/org.bootcontrol.Manager.service
D\-Bus activation service file.
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/org.bootcontrol.policy
Polkit action definitions.
.TP
.I /var/lib/bootcontrol/snapshots/
Pre-write snapshots, one subdirectory per operation.
.TP
.I /etc/bootcontrol/failsafe.cfg
Auto-regenerated GRUB failsafe entry.

.SH D-BUS INTERFACE
The daemon registers
.B org.bootcontrol.Manager
on
.IR /org/bootcontrol/Manager .
Methods (canonical PascalCase):
.IP \(bu 4
.B ReadGrubConfig
\(em return key=value dict and ETag.
.IP \(bu 4
.B SetGrubValue
\(em atomic write of a single key.
.IP \(bu 4
.B GetEtag
\(em current ETag of
.IR /etc/default/grub .
.IP \(bu 4
.B RebuildGrubConfig
\(em invoke
.BR grub-mkconfig (8).
.IP \(bu 4
.B ListLoaderEntries
\(em enumerate systemd-boot entries.
.IP \(bu 4
.B SetLoaderDefault
\(em set systemd-boot default entry.
.IP \(bu 4
.B ReadKernelCmdline
\(em params + ETag for
.IR /etc/kernel/cmdline
(or
.B rpm-ostree kargs
output on Fedora atomic hosts).
.IP \(bu 4
.B AddKernelParam
/
.B RemoveKernelParam
\(em mutate the kernel cmdline.
.IP \(bu 4
.B BackupNvram
\(em archive EFI NVRAM variables.
.IP \(bu 4
.B SignAndEnrollUki
\(em MOK signing path.
.IP \(bu 4
.B ListSnapshots
/
.B RestoreSnapshot
\(em snapshot enumeration and rollback.

Errors are propagated as structured D\-Bus names in the
.B org.bootcontrol.Error.*
namespace; clients match on the name, never on the message string.

